.TH SKOGAI-MODULE-SANDBOX 1  "skogai-module-sandbox 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-module\-sandbox \- an empty skogai to try things in: own layers, every module installed, skogai built
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai module sandbox\fR [OPTIONS] [DIR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
an empty skogai to try things in: own layers, every module installed, skogai built
.br

.br
makes <dir>/system and <dir>/global (the system and global layers) and a
.br
git repo <dir>/repo, installs every module found from here into its
.br
.skogai/modules (as `module add \-\-apply` would, from its source when it has
.br
one, else from where it was found) and builds skogai there.
.br
prints the env lines that switch a shell into it: no SKOGAI_* config from
.br
outside, the three layer dirs, the built skogai first on PATH, cd to repo.
.br
a dir made by an earlier sandbox is replaced; any other existing one is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR=\fISHELL\fR
.br
env lines for this shell, default from $SHELL
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRbash, zsh, fish]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
[\fIDIR\fR]
.br
default $TMPDIR/skogai
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
